  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> in vacuum is incident on a glass slab at angle <math><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and refracted at angle <math><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> along <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> as shown in the figure. The optical path length of light ray from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is:<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0181_57878498e7d2.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 212px;\" />"
  },
